Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:08:18 +0000
Subject: fix(compose): keep Android bounce on reverse lazy lists
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The reverse lazy native scroll patch forced bouncesEnable(false) on every
Android reverse list and re-synced any out-of-range native offset at once,
so a reverse list (for example a chat thread) could not be pulled past
either end. An Android over-scroll reports its translation as an offset
outside the native range; the scroll handlers already clamp that offset for
Compose, so the logical offset never moves. Keep that clamp, stop forcing
bounce off, and skip the immediate re-sync while an Android reverse list
bounces: native returns to the range by itself. The app's bouncesEnable
choice is honoured again, and other platforms and normal layouts keep the
previous behaviour.

Fork-Patch: compose-reverse-lazy-android-bounce
Origin: botiverse/mobile task #37 (thread edges cannot be pulled on Android)
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: Codex-Android-DevOPS (林舟) <codex-android-devops@agents.raft.build>

